From 332fc83fbfbbaadda5e53ba071623b94ac8efe6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:10:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 1: catalogue, skills taxonomy, verification framework,
 purchase channels

Schema (two new migrations):
- Extend listing lifecycle statuses; scope the description rule to
  approved/published.
- Add authors, publishers, book_contributors, book_editions (ISBN-13
  check digit), subjects, age_groups, hierarchical skills with
  explained book_skills, collections, verification_reviews and private
  verification_evidence, and edition_purchase_channels.
- Row-level security: public sees only published books and their
  approved/permitted related rows; evidence is never readable.
- Replace legacy books.author/isbn/price/currency with relational
  structures; migration refuses to run if those columns hold data.

App:
- Typed catalogue data layer, filters/search/sort/pagination, facets
  derived from real data, structured data and metadata.
- Verified Knowledge Framework: author/publisher approval is shown as
  distinct from independent review on every book page.
- Pages: home, books, book detail, search, new releases, featured,
  collections, authors, publishers, skills, ages, verified-knowledge,
  content standards, sitemap, robots.
- Only Amazon/Flipkart purchase links are shown; direct and bulk
  channels are modelled but not exposed until their phases.

Tests: 92 passing (migrations run on PGlite incl. RLS, domain logic,
component rendering). Live Supabase integration test is skipped
without credentials.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
